# Gallebo — Flight Sharing Platform

## Scope
- Develop phase-by-phase only. Do not implement features from future phases.
- Product docs: `../files/` (Flight documentation). Security doc governs server-only operations.

## Stack
- Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Supabase, MapLibre, Didit (later: Stripe, Resend).

## UI
- Use `docs/design-references/` (Wingly + AER). Primary layout = Wingly; premium accents = AER gold CTA and hero typography.
- Server Components by default. `"use client"` only when needed.
- Design: premium, clean, modern (lapa.ninja as secondary inspiration).

## Supabase
- RLS on all tables when they exist. Never use `service_role` on the client.
- Use generated types in `types/database.ts`.
- Sensitive ops: server client only; admin client in `lib/supabase/admin.ts` only.

## Security (server-only)
- Stripe webhooks, Didit API, IBAN decrypt, admin actions, email, cron, commission logic.
- Validate all inputs with Zod. `NEXT_PUBLIC_` only for public keys.

## Code quality
- No `any`. try/catch on async server code. No mock API data unless requested.
- No placeholder business logic except explicit phase-0 UI shells.
